One thing worth pointing out tonight amid the Binance hack is how fast the industry leading companies and executives moved.

Within about 40 minutes of the hot wallet drains starting, @tether and @circle had frozen funds tied to it.

@ethena posted within half an hour to tell users where its collateral sits, and shared its exposure about 20 minutes later.

@aave's USDT market on Ethereum was also frozen about an hour and a half in, according to onchain trackers, after the hacker started borrowing against it. (Note: Aave hasn't commented publicly yet)

There's still a lot up in the air, but seeing the industry move this quickly is a positive thing and hopefully means a lot of the funds can be recovered.

Praying for the best for Binance users and everyone involved 🙏

